"""Kieran Duffy, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 1 to 4 and 6).

Sources (Red Dead Wiki EN, Oct 2026, saved in scratchpad cov/kieran/ and cov/kieran/m/): character page "Kieran
Duffy" (Background, Events of Red Dead Redemption 2, Mission Appearances, Murders Committed, Trivia); FR page "Kieran
Duffy" (fr.txt); the only mission transcript on the wiki that involves him, "Old Friends/dialogues", plus "The
Aftermath of Genesis/dialogues" (Arthur and Charles talk about the prisoner) and "Who is Not Without Sin/dialogues"
(his one camp line, quoted in part C); mission pages (story, deaths, trivia, quote boxes) "Old Friends", "Paying a
Social Call" (no transcript on the wiki: none exists for this mission, checked Oct 2026), "Blood Feuds, Ancient and
Modern", "The Battle of Shady Belle", "No, No and Thrice, No" (Susan's remark), "Horsemen, Apocalypses" (no
transcript), "Goodbye, Dear Friend" (quote box); companion activity page "Fishing (Kieran Duffy)"; wiki pages "Six
Point Cabin" (Cumberland Forest, New Hanover), "Branwen" (his horse in the chase), "Camp Events" (stables at Colter,
apology to Abigail, the party, his disappearance), "Errand Boy" (burdock roots request).
Cross-checked against the fact-checked parts arthur_A/B/D, bill_A/B/C, john_A/D, dutch_A/C/D, charles_A/B/C,
abigail_A/B, jack_A/B, javier_B, hosea_B, micah_A, sadie_A: Dutch orders Bill to geld him and Bill takes up a pair of
red-hot tongs; Kieran rides to Six Point Cabin on John's horse; Bill's warning on the ride is attributed to the Red
Dead Wiki (bill_A); Arthur, Bill and John kill the sentries; Arthur takes the money from the chimney and the shotgun;
Micah and Kieran guard Clemens Point during "Blood Feuds"; Milton gives the gang three days conditional on Dutch's
surrender (uncle rules); Dutch has Charles, Swanson and Pearson bury Kieran while Arthur and John clear the bodies (the
mission page; the character page's "Swanson alone" version is dropped); Arthur's journal depends on honor (arthur_B).

Ownership: Personality, names ("O'Driscoll" as a nickname, the meaning of Ciaran and O Dubhthaigh), appearance,
weapons (custom Cattleman, knife), the horse Branwen as a mount, and camp scenes (Karen, Mary-Beth, Sadie, Tilly and
Jack while he is tied to the tree; the stables at Colter; Bill and the tongs, Bill and the bottle; Javier; Sean and
the Colm pronunciation and head-butt; the reading lesson; the apology to Abigail; the drunk talk with Arthur at the
party; Mary-Beth asking where he is; the reactions to his death of Bill, Charles, Uncle, Mary-Beth, Abigail, Molly,
Tilly and Micah) go to part B; this part refers to them in one clause at most. Part A OWNS the backstory he tells in
camp (father, cholera, stable, army, earlier outlaws, the O'Driscolls' offer), the burial, the grave and Arthur's
journal entries. Lines quoted in part C (Quotes) are paraphrased here without quotation marks: the name exchange in
"Old Friends", "a couple of months", "I hate that feller", the fishing quote box, John's "more like a teacher", Dutch's
"That poor boy, Kieran". Dutch's lines to him at Colter ("Welcome to your new home", "we shoot fellers as need
shooting") are paraphrased here and left to part B if it quotes them.

Excluded: the FR wiki's "tortured until he gives up the camp's location" and Wikipedia's matching sentence (from a
USgamer spoiler piece): the game never shows how the O'Driscolls found Shady Belle; Bill's "lose your balls first"
as a quotation (no transcript; paraphrased and attributed, as in bill_A); the "foreshadowing" of the eyes (interpretation);
Kieran sitting alone at night "because he does not feel accepted" (interpretation); Eastward Bound, Kieran thrown tied
among the supplies in a wagon (wiki trivia flagged "citation needed"); the IGN preview in which he was captured just
before "Paying a Social Call" (development, part D); the character page's claim that he "witnessed" the kidnapping
of Jack (he says so himself in a camp scene: told as his own account, in part B); Branwen "returning" to him
(horse, part B); the Saint Denis and Dullahan readings of his death (interpretation).
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no date of birth for Kieran. The Red Dead Wiki lists him as an American of Irish descent. What is known of his early life comes from his own account, given at the campfire to [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]] and on the fishing trip with [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]]. His father, an Irishman, hoped to farm in California. Both his parents died of cholera. Orphaned, he lost his job at a stable. He joined the army, an experience he says went badly. All of the outlaws he rode with next were killed. Fishing and looking after horses are among the very few things his father had time to teach him.",
              "Les jeux ne donnent aucune date de naissance pour Kieran. Le Red Dead Wiki le présente comme un Américain d'origine irlandaise. Ce que l'on sait de sa jeunesse vient de son propre récit, fait autour du feu à [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]] et pendant la partie de pêche avec [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]]. Son père, un Irlandais, espérait cultiver la terre en Californie. Ses deux parents meurent du choléra. Orphelin, il perd sa place dans une écurie. Il s'engage dans l'armée, une expérience qui, de son propre aveu, a mal tourné. Les hors-la-loi avec qui il chevauche ensuite finissent tous tués. La pêche et les soins aux chevaux comptent parmi les rares choses que son père a eu le temps de lui apprendre.")},
    {"p": two("Alone again, he crossed paths with the O'Driscoll Boys, the gang of [[colm-odriscoll|Colm O'Driscoll]] and the old rivals of the Van der Linde gang. According to his own account, they gave him the choice of riding with them or dying, which he says was no choice at all. He describes himself as the lowest-ranking member of the gang.",
              "De nouveau seul, il croise la route des O'Driscoll Boys, la bande de [[colm-odriscoll|Colm O'Driscoll]] et vieille rivale de la bande Van der Linde. D'après son propre récit, on lui laisse le choix entre les suivre et mourir, ce qui, dit-il, n'en était pas vraiment un. Il se décrit comme le dernier des derniers de la bande.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 1: Colter", "Chapitre 1 : Colter"), "chapter": 1},
    {"p": two("After the failed ferry robbery in Blackwater, the gang hides in the snow at Colter. In \"Old Friends\", [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] leads [[arthur-morgan|Arthur]], [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]], [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] southwest to an O'Driscoll camp near a lake, to raid it and find out about a robbery Colm is planning. From a ridge, Arthur and Dutch watch through binoculars as Colm strikes a young man, who rides out of the camp. Colm leaves soon after. The young man is Kieran. The gang wipes out the men left in the camp and drives off their reinforcements. On one of the bodies, Micah finds a plan concerning a train that belongs to [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]].",
              "Après l'échec du braquage du ferry à Blackwater, la bande se cache dans la neige à Colter. Dans \"Old Friends\", [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] emmène [[arthur-morgan|Arthur]], [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]], [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] vers le sud-ouest, jusqu'à un camp O'Driscoll installé près d'un lac, pour l'attaquer et découvrir le coup que prépare Colm. Depuis une crête, Arthur et Dutch observent à la jumelle Colm qui frappe un jeune homme ; celui-ci quitte le camp à cheval, et Colm part peu après. Ce jeune homme, c'est Kieran. La bande élimine les hommes restés au camp et repousse leurs renforts. Sur l'un des cadavres, Micah trouve un plan qui concerne un train appartenant à [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]].")},
    {"p": two("On the way back, Dutch spots a lone man standing in the snow near the lake and asks whether he was not the man with Colm. Arthur offers to deal with him, and Dutch tells him to bring the man back alive, since he could be useful. Kieran gets on his horse, Branwen, and flees. After a chase, Arthur ropes him out of the saddle and hogties him. Kieran claims Arthur has the wrong man. On the ride to Colter he first says he does not know his own name, then gives it. He begs to be let go and says he knows nothing real about the O'Driscolls, having ridden with them for only a couple of months. Arthur threatens to break every bone in his body, then forbids him to say another word.",
              "Sur le chemin du retour, Dutch aperçoit un homme seul, debout dans la neige près du lac, et demande si ce n'est pas celui qui se trouvait avec Colm. Arthur propose de s'en charger, et Dutch lui demande de le ramener vivant, car il pourrait servir. Kieran saute sur son cheval, Branwen, et s'enfuit. Au terme d'une poursuite, Arthur le fait tomber de selle au lasso et le ligote. Kieran prétend qu'Arthur se trompe de personne. Pendant le trajet vers Colter, il commence par dire qu'il ne connaît pas son propre nom, puis finit par le donner. Il supplie qu'on le relâche et jure qu'il ne sait rien de sérieux sur les O'Driscoll, avec qui il ne roule que depuis deux ou trois mois. Arthur menace de lui briser tous les os du corps, puis lui interdit de dire un mot de plus.")},
    {"p": two("At Colter, Arthur drops him on the ground in front of Dutch and offers to make him talk. Dutch refuses: \"Oh no, now all we'll get is lies.\" He has Bill and [[uncle|Uncle]] tie the prisoner up somewhere safe and says they will get him hungry first. As he is carried off, Kieran protests that he is not an O'Driscoll and that he hates Colm; Dutch answers with sarcasm. He is kept tied up in the stable of the Colter camp (see Relationships). In \"The Aftermath of Genesis\", if it is played after \"Old Friends\", Arthur tells [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] on a hunting trip that they will feed the O'Driscoll nothing but the can of salted offal [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] gave them. When Charles suggests that [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] might deal with the prisoner herself, Arthur laughs, then says the man is weak, which makes him all the more useful.",
              "À Colter, Arthur le jette à terre devant Dutch et propose de le faire parler. Dutch refuse : on n'en tirerait plus que des mensonges, dit-il. Il charge Bill et [[uncle|Uncle]] d'attacher le prisonnier en lieu sûr et annonce qu'on va d'abord lui donner faim. Pendant qu'on l'emmène, Kieran proteste qu'il n'est pas un O'Driscoll et qu'il déteste Colm ; Dutch lui répond avec ironie. Il reste attaché dans l'écurie du camp de Colter (voir Relations). Dans \"The Aftermath of Genesis\", si la mission est jouée après \"Old Friends\", Arthur explique à [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]], pendant une partie de chasse, qu'on ne donnera rien à manger à l'O'Driscoll, sauf peut-être la boîte d'abats salés offerte par [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]]. Quand Charles suggère que [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] pourrait bien régler son compte au prisonnier, Arthur rit, puis ajoute que l'homme est faible, ce qui le rend d'autant plus utile.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 2: Horseshoe Overlook", "Chapitre 2 : Horseshoe Overlook"), "chapter": 2},
    {"p": two("When the gang moves down to Horseshoe Overlook, above Valentine, Kieran comes too, still a prisoner. He spends close to a month tied to a tree in the camp, thin and weak, where several members of the gang taunt him or bring him water (see Relationships). In \"Paying a Social Call\", Arthur questions him about the O'Driscolls, and Kieran says he knows nothing. Dutch and Bill join them. Dutch orders Bill to geld the prisoner on the spot, and Bill takes up a pair of red-hot tongs. Kieran gives way before Bill can use them: he says that Colm is holed up at Six Point Cabin, an O'Driscoll hideout in Cumberland Forest, and offers to take them there. Arthur sets off with Bill and [[john-marston|John Marston]], Kieran riding behind John on his horse.",
              "Quand la bande s'installe à Horseshoe Overlook, au-dessus de Valentine, Kieran suit, toujours prisonnier. Il passe près d'un mois attaché à un arbre au milieu du camp, amaigri et affaibli, où plusieurs membres de la bande se moquent de lui ou lui apportent de l'eau (voir Relations). Dans \"Paying a Social Call\", Arthur l'interroge sur les O'Driscoll, et Kieran répond qu'il ne sait rien. Dutch et Bill les rejoignent. Dutch ordonne à Bill de castrer le prisonnier sur-le-champ, et Bill s'empare d'une pince chauffée au rouge. Kieran craque avant que Bill ne s'en serve : Colm, dit-il, se terre à Six Point Cabin, une planque des O'Driscoll dans la forêt de Cumberland, et il propose de les y conduire. Arthur part avec Bill et [[john-marston|John Marston]], Kieran monté derrière John sur son cheval.")},
    {"p": two("On the ride, Bill tells Arthur that he has slipped throwing knives into his saddle, and, according to the Red Dead Wiki, warns Kieran that if he turns on them he will lose his manhood before his life. Kieran says that the O'Driscolls and the Van der Linde gang are not so different, and John replies that he knows nothing about them. If the player talks to neither John nor Bill, John complains about Kieran's smell after weeks tied to a tree, then brings up Colm's murder of Annabelle, Dutch's lover, and reproaches Kieran for riding with a man who kills women. At Six Point Cabin, Arthur, Bill and John kill the sentries quietly, one of them as he relieves himself against a tree, then defeat the rest of the O'Driscolls in a gunfight.",
              "En chemin, Bill apprend à Arthur qu'il a glissé des couteaux de lancer dans sa selle et, d'après le Red Dead Wiki, prévient Kieran qu'une trahison lui coûterait sa virilité avant de lui coûter la vie. Kieran fait remarquer que les O'Driscoll et la bande Van der Linde ne sont pas si différents, et John lui rétorque qu'il ne sait rien d'eux. Si le joueur ne parle ni à John ni à Bill, John se plaint de l'odeur de Kieran après des semaines passées attaché à un arbre, puis évoque le meurtre d'Annabelle, la compagne de Dutch, par Colm, et reproche à Kieran d'avoir suivi un homme qui tue les femmes. À Six Point Cabin, Arthur, Bill et John éliminent les sentinelles en silence, dont une en train d'uriner contre un arbre, puis viennent à bout des autres O'Driscoll dans une fusillade.")},
    {"p": two("Arthur then goes into the cabin at the back of the camp, expecting to find Colm there. A last O'Driscoll throws him to the floor as he enters, and Kieran shoots the man dead, saving Arthur's life. Colm is not in the cabin, and Arthur, convinced that Kieran has led them into a trap, points his gun at him. Kieran points out that he has just saved Arthur's life, and Bill backs him. Arthur then tells him he has earned his freedom and can go. Kieran refuses: alone, with Colm's men after him, he would not last long, and letting him go would amount to killing him. Pressed by Bill and John, Arthur agrees to let him join the gang and sends him back to camp with them. Arthur then takes the money Kieran had mentioned from the chimney, and a shotgun from above the fireplace.",
              "Arthur entre ensuite dans la cabane, au fond du camp, persuadé d'y trouver Colm. Un dernier O'Driscoll le renverse dès le seuil, et Kieran abat l'homme, sauvant la vie d'Arthur. Colm n'est pas dans la cabane, et Arthur, convaincu que Kieran les a menés dans un piège, le met en joue. Kieran lui rappelle qu'il vient de lui sauver la vie, et Bill lui donne raison. Arthur lui annonce alors qu'il a gagné sa liberté et peut partir. Kieran refuse : seul, avec les hommes de Colm à ses trousses, il ne tiendrait pas longtemps, et le relâcher reviendrait à le tuer. Sous l'insistance de Bill et de John, Arthur accepte qu'il rejoigne la bande et le renvoie au camp avec eux. Arthur récupère ensuite dans la cheminée l'argent dont Kieran avait parlé, ainsi qu'un fusil posé au-dessus de l'âtre.")},
    {"p": two("From then on, Kieran is a member of the gang, though not a trusted one (see Relationships). According to the Red Dead Wiki, three O'Driscolls met near the hotel in Valentine after this mission recognize Arthur as a man who has been riding with Kieran Duffy. In \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Kieran is one of the people in camp who comment when Arthur carries a drunk [[orville-swanson|Reverend Swanson]] back to his tent. At the end of the chapter, after \"A Strange Kindness\", the gang leaves for Clemens Point, on Flat Iron Lake in Lemoyne, and Kieran moves with it.",
              "Kieran fait désormais partie de la bande, sans en avoir la confiance (voir Relations). D'après le Red Dead Wiki, trois O'Driscoll croisés près de l'hôtel de Valentine après cette mission reconnaissent en Arthur un homme qui chevauche avec Kieran Duffy. Dans \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Kieran fait partie de ceux qui réagissent au camp quand Arthur ramène sous sa tente le [[orville-swanson|révérend Swanson]], ivre. À la fin du chapitre, après \"A Strange Kindness\", la bande part pour Clemens Point, au bord du lac Flat Iron, en Lemoyne, et Kieran la suit.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("At Clemens Point, after \"The New South\", Kieran offers Arthur a fishing trip, a companion activity. The two ride to the shore of Radley's Pasture, on Flat Iron Lake, with Kieran on Branwen, and Kieran remarks that not long ago he was tied to the back of Arthur's horse, begging for mercy. A naked swimmer comes out of the water and tells them about an unusually large fish further along the shore. At the new spot, Arthur can catch the Legendary Bluegill with a special lake lure. Kieran rides back to camp once the fish is caught or, if it is not, after a while, leaving Arthur on the shore.",
              "À Clemens Point, après \"The New South\", Kieran propose à Arthur une partie de pêche, une activité de compagnon. Les deux hommes rejoignent la rive de Radley's Pasture, sur le lac Flat Iron, Kieran sur Branwen, et Kieran fait remarquer qu'il n'y a pas si longtemps, il était ligoté sur le cheval d'Arthur à implorer sa pitié. Un baigneur nu sort de l'eau et leur parle d'un poisson d'une taille inhabituelle un peu plus loin sur la rive. Au nouvel emplacement, Arthur peut attraper le crapet arlequin légendaire avec un leurre spécial pour lac. Kieran rentre au camp une fois la prise faite ou, à défaut, au bout d'un moment, et laisse Arthur au bord de l'eau.")},
    {"p": two("After the Rhodes ambush in which Sean is killed, [[abigail-marston|Abigail Marston]] tells Arthur that [[jack-marston|Jack]] has disappeared, and the gang concludes that the Braithwaites have taken him. In \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", Dutch, Arthur, [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]], John, Charles, Bill, Javier and Lenny ride to Braithwaite Manor, while Micah and Kieran are left behind to guard the camp. According to the character page of the Red Dead Wiki, he is among the gang members present the next morning, in \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", when the Pinkerton agents [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] and [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] come to Clemens Point. Milton offers a deal: if Dutch comes with him, the others get three days to disappear. The gang refuses, and the agents leave. The gang moves to Shady Belle, an abandoned plantation house in the bayou near Saint Denis.",
              "Après l'embuscade de Rhodes où Sean est tué, [[abigail-marston|Abigail Marston]] annonce à Arthur que [[jack-marston|Jack]] a disparu, et la bande en conclut que les Braithwaite l'ont enlevé. Dans \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", Dutch, Arthur, [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]], John, Charles, Bill, Javier et Lenny chevauchent jusqu'au manoir Braithwaite, tandis que Micah et Kieran restent garder le camp. D'après la page du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki, il fait partie des membres de la bande présents le lendemain matin, dans \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", quand les agents de la Pinkerton [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] et [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] se présentent à Clemens Point. Milton propose un marché : si Dutch le suit, les autres auront trois jours pour disparaître. La bande refuse, et les agents repartent. La bande s'installe à Shady Belle, une demeure de plantation abandonnée dans le bayou, près de Saint-Denis.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("Kieran takes no part in the main events of the chapter. At Shady Belle, he goes to Abigail to apologize for failing to see the kidnapping coming (see Relationships). After Jack is brought back from [[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]]'s mansion in \"Angelo Bronte, A Man of Honor\", the gang throws a party. Kieran first watches from a distance, then, encouraged by [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]] and Arthur, drinks, and he talks to Arthur once he is drunk (see Relationships). He disappears from the camp right after the party. In \"No, No and Thrice, No\", if the mission is played after Jack's return, [[susan-grimshaw|Susan Grimshaw]] remarks to Arthur on the ride that nobody has seen Kieran for a while.",
              "Kieran ne prend aucune part aux grands événements du chapitre. À Shady Belle, il va s'excuser auprès d'Abigail de ne pas avoir vu venir l'enlèvement (voir Relations). Après le retour de Jack, tiré de la demeure d'[[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]] dans \"Angelo Bronte, A Man of Honor\", la bande fait la fête. Kieran regarde d'abord de loin puis, poussé par [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]] et par Arthur, se met à boire, et parle à Arthur une fois ivre (voir Relations). Il disparaît du camp juste après la fête. Dans \"No, No and Thrice, No\", si la mission est jouée après le retour de Jack, [[susan-grimshaw|Susan Grimshaw]] fait remarquer à Arthur, en chemin, que personne n'a vu Kieran depuis un moment.")},
    {"p": two("\"Horsemen, Apocalypses\" opens with Dutch and Arthur planning the trolley station robbery Bronte has suggested. Dutch notices a strange rider coming into camp. [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] screams when she recognizes Kieran. He is dead on the horse: the O'Driscolls have cut off his head, gouged out his eyes and tied the body so that the head rests in his own hands. A large band of O'Driscolls attacks Shady Belle immediately afterwards. Arthur fires from the balcony, then joins the fight at the front door. Overwhelmed, the gang falls back into the house and barricades the door, and Sadie kills several attackers on her own at the back of the house. The surviving O'Driscolls flee.",
              "\"Horsemen, Apocalypses\" s'ouvre sur Dutch et Arthur en train de préparer l'attaque de la gare de tramways que leur a soufflée Bronte. Dutch remarque un cavalier étrange qui entre dans le camp. [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] hurle en reconnaissant Kieran. Il est mort sur le cheval : les O'Driscoll l'ont décapité, lui ont arraché les yeux et ont attaché le corps de façon que la tête repose entre ses mains. Une bande nombreuse d'O'Driscoll attaque Shady Belle dans la foulée. Arthur tire depuis le balcon, puis rejoint le combat devant la porte d'entrée. Débordée, la bande se replie dans la maison et barricade la porte, et Sadie abat à elle seule plusieurs assaillants derrière la maison. Les O'Driscoll survivants prennent la fuite.")},
    {"p": two("After the fight, Dutch has Charles, Reverend Swanson and Pearson bury Kieran, while Arthur and John clear away the bodies of the attackers. According to the Red Dead Wiki, his grave lies in a meadow west of Shady Belle. Arthur's journal entry depends on his honor. With high honor, he regrets that he could not save Kieran, who had once saved his own life, and writes that he will miss him. With low honor, he only describes the beheading, the attack and his dislike of the swamps. In the hours after the battle, several members of the gang talk to Arthur about Kieran's death, among them Bill, Charles, Mary-Beth, Abigail, [[molly-oshea|Molly O'Shea]] and Micah (see Relationships).",
              "Après le combat, Dutch charge Charles, le révérend Swanson et Pearson d'enterrer Kieran, pendant qu'Arthur et John évacuent les corps des assaillants. D'après le Red Dead Wiki, sa tombe se trouve dans une prairie à l'ouest de Shady Belle. L'entrée du journal d'Arthur dépend de son honneur. Avec un honneur élevé, il regrette de n'avoir pas pu sauver Kieran, qui lui avait sauvé la vie, et écrit qu'il lui manquera. Avec un honneur bas, il se borne à décrire la décapitation, l'attaque et son aversion pour les marais. Dans les heures qui suivent, plusieurs membres de la bande parlent à Arthur de la mort de Kieran, dont Bill, Charles, Mary-Beth, Abigail, [[molly-oshea|Molly O'Shea]] et Micah (voir Relations).")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 6: Beaver Hollow", "Chapitre 6 : Beaver Hollow"), "chapter": 6},
    {"p": two("Colm O'Driscoll is later arrested and sentenced to hang in Saint Denis. In \"Goodbye, Dear Friend\", because Colm has already escaped the noose twice, Dutch and Sadie decide to attend the execution in disguise and bring Arthur with them. Before the hanging, Dutch reminds Sadie of what each of them has lost because of Colm: her husband, his Annabelle, and Kieran. Dutch, Arthur and Sadie stop an O'Driscoll attempt to free their leader, and Colm is hanged.",
              "Colm O'Driscoll est ensuite arrêté et condamné à la pendaison à Saint-Denis. Dans \"Goodbye, Dear Friend\", comme Colm a déjà échappé deux fois à la corde, Dutch et Sadie décident d'assister à l'exécution déguisés et emmènent Arthur. Avant la pendaison, Dutch rappelle à Sadie ce que chacun d'eux a perdu à cause de Colm : son mari à elle, son Annabelle à lui, et Kieran. Dutch, Arthur et Sadie font échouer une tentative des O'Driscoll pour libérer leur chef, et Colm est pendu.")},
]
